 knowing a command line exists.
 
+## When it is taken, and what that costs
+
+**A shape that looks like `⟨n,m,k⟩` is quotiented by default.** No `--symmetry`
+word means `Inferred`: the three dimensions are read as `nm x mk x kn`, whose
+product is `(nmk)^2`, and where they come out whole the closed-form group is
+used. A shape that is not a product gets no group, and one that looks like a
+product and is not gets a small stabiliser rather than a wrong one, because
+`stabiliser_of` keeps only what actually fixes `span(T)`. `-s none` turns it off,
+which is how the two are timed against each other on one question.
+
+**It is not free on a satisfiable question, and the direction is measured.** On
+`matmul_2x2x2`, one core:
+
+| question | quotiented | `-s none` | |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `--target 6`, refute | 648 nodes, 0.0161 s | 25 399 nodes, 0.0368 s | 39x nodes, **2.3x faster** |
+| `--target 7`, find | 3 167 nodes, 0.1545 s | 7 436 nodes, 0.0210 s | 2.3x nodes, **7.4x slower** |
+
+The quotient costs about 17 us a node against 2.8 us, spent striking orbits and
+narrowing the residual subgroup. A refutation visits the whole tree, so 39x fewer
+nodes pays for it. A find stops at the first witness in index order, so the plain
+search gets there before the quotient has earned its per-node cost back. **This is
+the same asymmetry `orbit_cubes` measures on the solver**, where cubes are worth
+8.2x on a refutation and 250x worse on a find, and it has the same cause.
+
+Both rows are milliseconds, so they say which way the effect goes and not how
+large it is. A question with real weight has not been measured either way.
+
+**The sweep is not affected.** `fewest_products_by_sweep` has no quotiented form,
+so `decide-rank` with no `--target` runs exactly as it did. Giving the sweep one
+is what would let this default be right rather than a coin flip, since a sweep is
+every refutation below the answer and one find at the end.
+
 ## What it is worth, measured
 
 Refuting `⟨2,2,2⟩` at k = 6 costs the tree search **0.56 s plain and 0.02 s
